-- title:
--   Base change to ℂ of a curve model, compatibly with places
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $M$ and write $R=\mathbb{Z}[1/M]$ for the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ away from $M$. Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a morphism $\pi_X : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ that is proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ and all of whose geometric fibres are integral, in the sense that the pullback of $\pi_X$ along any morphism $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ with $k$ an algebraically closed field is integral. Let $\bar s : \operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism, and let $\bar F$ be a field extension of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is essentially of finite type and satisfies `IsCurveOver`: every nonzero element of $\bar F$ is the function of a degree-zero divisor recording its orders at all places, every place has residue field finite over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\Omega_{\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ is free of rank $1$ over $\bar F$. Let $\mathfrak{M}$ be a curve model of $\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. an integral scheme $\mathfrak{M}.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, together with an isomorphism of $\bar F$ with its function field over the base, a bijection from the closed points of $\mathfrak{M}.C$ to the places of $\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identifying stalks with valuation subrings, and the property that every finite set of points lies in an affine open. Let $e_{\mathfrak{M}} : \mathfrak{M}.C \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (pullback of $\pi_X$ along $\bar s$) be an isomorphism whose composition with the second projection is $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{toBase}$. Let $\iota : \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism, let $F_c$ be a field extension of $\mathbb{C}$ that is essentially of finite type and satisfies the same `IsCurveOver` conditions, and let $t : \bar F \to F_c$ be a ring homomorphism and $P \mapsto P_{\mathbb{C}}$ a map from places of $\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of $F_c/\mathbb{C}$ such that: $t$ is compatible with $\iota$ on constants; the subfield of $F_c$ generated by $\mathbb{C}$ together with the image of $t$ is all of $F_c$; $t$ carries every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-linearly independent finite subset of $\bar F$ to a $\mathbb{C}$-linearly independent family; and for every place $P$ and every $x \in \bar F$ one has $t(x)$ in the valuation subring of $P_{\mathbb{C}}$ exactly when $x$ lies in that of $P$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a curve model $\mathfrak{M}_c$ of $F_c/\mathbb{C}$ and an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak{M}_c}$ from $\mathfrak{M}_c.C$ to the pullback of $\pi_X$ along $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota)$ followed by $\bar s$, whose composition with the second projection is $\mathfrak{M}_c.\mathrm{toBase}$, and such that for every place $P$ of $\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the $\mathbb{C}$-point of $X$ obtained from the section corresponding to $P_{\mathbb{C}}$ under $\mathfrak{M}_c.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ (composed with $e_{\mathfrak{M}_c}$ and the first projection) agrees with $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota)$ followed by the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $X$ obtained from the section corresponding to $P$ under $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$.
--
--   This is the base-change (constant field extension) statement for curves: the complex fibre $X_{\mathbb{C}}$ of an arithmetic surface over $\mathbb{Z}[1/M]$ is again a smooth proper integral curve, it is a curve model of the constant field extension $F_c$ of the function field $\bar F$ of $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$, and the dictionary between points and places commutes with the extension $P \mapsto P_{\mathbb{C}}$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development to transfer statements about $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of a Hecke curve to the complex-analytic side, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_period_algEquiv_pt_iff_bcPlace_of_uniformizedHeckeCurve_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_period_algEquiv_pt_iff_bcPlace_of_uniformizedHeckeCurve_of_two_mul_dvd).
